SUMMARY:Pier Park Pick-Up
DESCRIPTION:We will be removing invasives like ivy and blackberry\, picking up litter\, dragging fallen limbs into piles\, and weeding the new beds of native plant to help give them a good start. All ages and families are welcome. Work begins at 9 am with a short orientation talk and finishes up about noon. Wear good work shoes and be prepared for the weather. If you have them\, bring your own work gloves and a container for water. We will have fresh water to fill your containers. Friends of Pier Park will also provide coffee and donuts for all volunteers. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/pier-park-pick-up/
LOCATION:Pier Park-meeting at the intersection of N Bruce and N James St.\, Meet at the blacktop trail leading into the park from the farthest parking lot. Follow N Kelley Point Park Road to the end.
CATEGORIES:Kids Calendar,Outdoor,Plants & Nature
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/Pier-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="SOLVE":MAILTO:peter@solveoregon.org
END:VEVENT
